WEBVTT

1
00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:13.202
Mandy looked closer at Leo's writing.

2
00:00:13.203 --> 00:00:17.072
"Can you read this, Vinnie?" she said.

3
00:00:17.073 --> 00:00:20.411
But Vinnie was looking at the photo.

4
00:00:20.412 --> 00:00:22.912
It was glowing blue.

5
00:00:22.913 --> 00:00:26.980
They were standing where the old man had stood!

6
00:00:26.981 --> 00:00:31.343
A well-dressed woman suddenly walked past the children.

7
00:00:31.344 --> 00:00:34.117
She seemed to be in a rush.

8
00:00:34.118 --> 00:00:39.658
As she hurried toward the cathedral door, something fell from her neck.

9
00:00:39.659 --> 00:00:44.259
It landed softly on the open page of Leo's notebook.

10
00:00:44.260 --> 00:00:47.082
It was a mirror locket.

11
00:00:47.083 --> 00:00:50.952
Mandy noticed the small mirror on the notebook.

12
00:00:50.953 --> 00:00:55.557
"Vinnie, look!" she whispered excitedly.

13
00:00:55.558 --> 00:01:00.097
She picked up the book and held the mirror to the page.

14
00:01:00.098 --> 00:01:03.522
Now Mandy could read the writing!

15
00:01:03.523 --> 00:01:10.136
"The thoughts and ideas of Leonardo di ser Piero da Vinci!" she read.

16
00:01:10.137 --> 00:01:15.187
"Leonardo da Vinci!" the children shouted.

17
00:01:15.188 --> 00:01:21.512
The photo glowed red as they fell down the dark tunnel.

18
00:01:21.513 --> 00:01:25.011
They landed with a thump in the attic.

19
00:01:25.012 --> 00:01:29.592
"Wow, the greatest artist of all time!

20
00:01:29.593 --> 00:01:35.097
It's too bad we didn't get to talk to him more!" cried Mandy.

21
00:01:35.098 --> 00:01:38.919
"I could tell he was special," said Vinnie.

22
00:01:38.920 --> 00:01:42.084
Mandy rolled her eyes.

23
00:01:42.085 --> 00:01:47.540
"Vinnie! Mandy! Come downstairs!" shouted Mom.

24
00:01:47.541 --> 00:01:52.478
The children ran down to their parents, who were still in the kitchen.

25
00:01:52.479 --> 00:01:55.855
"We need to talk," said Mom.

26
00:01:55.856 --> 00:01:59.623
The children sat quietly and listened.

27
00:01:59.624 --> 00:02:03.186
"We're moving again," began Dad.

28
00:02:03.187 --> 00:02:06.263
"The company needs me in California."

29
00:02:06.264 --> 00:02:10.975
"California!" the children shouted together.

30
00:02:10.976 --> 00:02:15.354
"We just moved here!" said Vinnie.

31
00:02:15.355 --> 00:02:20.912
"I know," said Dad. "But this can't be helped."

32
00:02:20.913 --> 00:02:25.830
For the next few days, the children were busy packing.

33
00:02:25.831 --> 00:02:29.241
"Kids, would you mind clearing out the attic for me?"

34
00:02:29.242 --> 00:02:31.697
Dad asked one morning.

35
00:02:31.698 --> 00:02:36.516
With heavy hearts Vinnie and Mandy went upstairs.

36
00:02:36.517 --> 00:02:40.634
"I'm sad to leave," cried Mandy.

37
00:02:40.635 --> 00:02:46.305
"Well, at least we got to the end of the album," said Vinnie.

38
00:02:46.306 --> 00:02:49.090
He took the album out again.

39
00:02:49.091 --> 00:02:52.721
Each page had a photo of their travels.

40
00:02:52.722 --> 00:02:58.950
In the pictures the old man was gone, replaced by Vinnie and Mandy.

41
00:02:58.951 --> 00:03:02.404
The objects were not glowing anymore.

42
00:03:02.405 --> 00:03:06.774
"We had some great adventures," said Vinnie.

43
00:03:06.775 --> 00:03:11.143
"And we made many friends," added Mandy.

44
00:03:11.144 --> 00:03:14.481
"What was your favorite journey?"

45
00:03:14.482 --> 00:03:17.148
Vinnie thought for a moment.

46
00:03:17.149 --> 00:03:19.183
"I liked every one.

47
00:03:19.184 --> 00:03:25.440
I learned so much about the world—its different people and their special cultures."

48
00:03:25.441 --> 00:03:29.286
"Me too," agreed Mandy.

49
00:03:29.287 --> 00:03:32.589
"What should we do now?" asked Vinnie.

50
00:03:32.590 --> 00:03:35.317
The children sat and thought.

51
00:03:35.318 --> 00:03:39.713
"Someone else will be living here, right?" said Mandy.

52
00:03:39.714 --> 00:03:42.728
"Maybe they'll find this album.

53
00:03:42.729 --> 00:03:46.725
Maybe they'll go on photo travels too."

54
00:03:46.726 --> 00:03:50.392
"Should we leave a note?" asked Vinnie.

55
00:03:50.393 --> 00:03:53.801
"Great idea!" Mandy said.

56
00:03:53.802 --> 00:03:58.806
She grabbed a pen and turned to the first page of the album.

57
00:03:58.807 --> 00:04:05.240
"On our first trip to Egypt, a glowing pyramid called to us . . . ," Mandy wrote.

58
00:04:05.241 --> 00:04:09.616
They finished the note and closed the photo album.

59
00:04:09.617 --> 00:04:13.519
Then they put it in a corner of the attic.

60
00:04:13.520 --> 00:04:18.005
A week later, the family shut the door of their house.

61
00:04:18.006 --> 00:04:21.968
Vinnie and Mandy looked up at the attic window.

62
00:04:21.969 --> 00:04:27.372
Exciting adventures were waiting for whoever would find the album next.

63
00:04:27.373 --> 00:04:37.108
For Vinnie and Mandy, another adventure was about to begin.

64
00:04:37.110 --> 00:05:22.190
[caption_out@
